<<~ kanawai uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119`>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Affordance ~ one carrier per affordance address

An ''affordance carrier'' describes one thing the house affords: its arguments, its examples, its gate, its refusals with their cures, its answers, and every door that reaches it. A CLI verb, an MCP tool, a TW5 action widget and a console call each stand as a ''skin'' of one carrier and hold no words of their own; each renders the carrier. One filter on the address gathers the carrier, its code, its tests, its canon law and its act records, so two doors for one power show as two skins under one address, in plain sight.

''A carrier describes; it never grants'' (Domain Affordances law 1). No slot, field or tag of a carrier feeds an admission check. `#/gate` carries testimony of the gate; the door checks the ocap. A drift law compares the testimony to the handler, never the reverse.

The type tag `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance`, written fully qualified, gathers every carrier: `[tag[lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance]]` derives the Affordance Map, and no table lists it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/residency`>>

!! residency ~ address tag · stable seat · canon bag · role

''The address.'' An affordance address takes the three-term root of the `lar:` URI law (`lar:///library.oracle.speaks`: heading, angle, dynamic), held to the seed headings at t1. A carrier never names a wildcard as its own address; `library.*` rides a help filter alone.

''The seat (measured in source, 2026-11-26).'' The canon walk seats a carrier only at a `uri-path` that opens on a three-term root FOLLOWED BY a path: the siting function (`carrierBaseRelPath`, `lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts`) answers null for a bare root, the genesis cut then refuses the carrier as a title/path disagreement (`genesis-floor.ts`), and the mirror's reverse derivation (`mirrorDirFileToUri`) skips the file. The daemon working layer seats a bare-root title through the tiddler door; canon and genesis do not. So a canon carrier seats at the stable path `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/<address terms>` and TAGS its bare address:

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`seat` name=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/library.oracle.speaks` params=`tags/lar:///library.oracle.speaks ~ the carrier of the oracle consult`>>
```

`[tag[lar:///library.oracle.speaks]]` then gathers carrier, code, tests and every cast record under one spelling. Where the siting function learns the bare root, the carrier moves to the bare title whole, and the stable seat leaves as a forwarder.

''A bare root resolves; the stack decides (`carrierOf`, `lararium-tw5/src/affordance-read.ts`).'' Every read of an address runs over the caller's view of the whole bag stack, working layers included, and names the carrier that answered: a record titled with the bare root wins where any layer holds one; else the stable seat answers (`lares`, then `lararium`); else a carrier that tags the address. TiddlyWiki's own shadow cascade picks the topmost layer for either title. A get of `lar:///library.oracle.speaks` that no record titles reads the carrier at its seat, `address` naming the root and the has line's `layer/` naming the bag that seated it; the `afford` filter operator, `$tw.lares.afford` and the skin templates read through the same resolve. So a spirit or an operator re-shapes a door by seating a carrier above canon (at the seat, or at the bare root), behavior slots included, and `delete mode=reveal` returns canon's. No fence guards a carrier: the door's ocap check, receipt and base guard hold as for any record.

''A slot put over a canon family (measured 2026-11-27, stack#1: the floor build's door over a read-only canon layer and a working layer, in one process under a scratch root; the probe modelled the island adaptor's routing of each non-foam change to the working layer, so a live vessel's shore gives the confirming read).'' A text put on one slot of a family whose every member rests in read-only canon answers `decision: put` in the working bag, and the Confluence gate re-lands the whole family in the wiki (`landed` names every member). Only the members the wiki now holds otherwise than canon move: the edited slot and the root (its reseal moves its record). Under the shore's foam rule those two copy up to the working layer, and every untouched slot stays in canon by reference, so the family stands split across two layers and recomposes whole under a new canonical hash, the root's has line naming the working layer. A field put on the root copies up the root alone. A family reveal (`family: true`, `mode: reveal`) retracts the working members and canon's carrier returns byte for byte, its canonical hash equal to the one read before the put. A first edit copies up what it moves, never the whole family.

''Routes, loops and cures read the live stack; the pack holds the floor.'' Spelling to address, per surface, derives from the `#/skins` of the carrier that answers each address over the caller's view (`routesOf`, `lararium-tw5/src/affordance-read.ts`), so a working-layer skin row moves a route and a reveal returns canon's. A bare-root carrier a layer seats with no type tag joins by its `#/skins` slots alone; a record that skins no surface (an alias) routes nothing. A verb that lands an act record reads its `#/loop` rows from the same carrier first. The baked pack (`affordance-pack.json`) runs the same derivation over canon and keeps its content hash: it stands as the floor a sleeping vessel answers from, and answers in the stack's place only where the stack answers nothing. Every answer names the carrier that answered, `carrier/<title> bag/<bag> base/<hash>` on its has line; the floor names itself `bag/pack base/<pack hash>`.

''A renamed address (early alpha).'' A rename moves the carrier whole to its new seat and sweeps every reference; no alias record stands at the old address, which answers nothing (the operator's word 2026-11-27: alpha burns aliases, never flags them off). The signed alias record of Domain Affordances law 4 waits on the pono guards' return.

''The bag'' follows the package that owns the handler: `lares` for the house's own, `lararium` for mesh affordances. Placement chooses residency; the title never does.

''Meta.'' `role` holds the one line, written from the verb, 72 characters or fewer, so the has-stack's root line reads whole as the short help. `l-space = "stable"` and `cacheable = true` ride every carrier.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/slots`>>

!! slots ~ head · shows · takes · gate · refuses · answers · loop · skins · edges

The slot set stays closed and runs in loop order, so a paged whole-read, cut on slot boundaries, stops at a phase edge. An absent slot says "nothing to say here", never a fault, except `#/head` and `#/skins`.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/head` params=`phase/✶ row/prose ~ the one line, then a synopsis: what the house does here, its record, its radius`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/shows` params=`phase/✶ row/example ~ examples as neutral calls each skin renders runnable`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/takes` params=`phase/⏿ row/arg ~ every argument, surface-neutral`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/gate` params=`phase/◇ row/gate ~ testimony: seat or hand, the ocap species asked, whether the act holds a key`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/refuses` params=`phase/◇ row/refusal ~ every refusal code, each with its cure as a neutral call`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/answers` params=`phase/▶ row/band ~ every band the act answers, its exit class and its envelope fields`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/loop` params=`phase/▶ row/kahea ~ the act shape: a call to the law that owns the procedure`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/skins` params=`phase/↺ row/skin ~ one nested slot per surface: the spelling, and only the names that break the rule`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/edges` params=`phase/↺ row/loulou ~ the canon law the affordance enacts, and its tests' law module`>>
```

''Every slot leads with a digest line'' (`!! takes ~ recipe · asking · observe`), so the card lists argument names, refusal codes and surfaces before any slot unfolds. An author writes the digest; a check law reds where it drifts from the rows beneath.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rows`>>

!! rows ~ arg · cell · band · refusal · example · gate · skin

Rows ride the `has` grammar and its `key/value` params; `[[…]]` brackets a value holding spaces; the tagline after `~` carries the row's one line.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`asking` params=`takes/words needs/seat ~ the query, named before the throw`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`fresh` params=`gate/hand ~ throw anew for the same words`>>
<<has entity=`cell` name=`?` params=`mu/relate ~ the card: the has line, its size and its base`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`asks` params=`exit/5 ~ a seat asked what a hand alone gives; the line a person runs rides the answer`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`oracle-cast-untimed` params=`cure/[[library.oracle.speaks at/<time>]] ~ the verb reads no clock`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`first-cast` params=`recipe/default asking/[[which lane lands first]] ~ a seat's cast at its own open fork`>>
<<has entity=`gate` name=`coins` params=`who/hand ~ a person's own throw; a seat's coins answer asks`>>
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`spells/[[lares oracle cast]] ~ the terminal`>>
```

* ''An arg with no `takes/` reads as a boolean flag.'' `needs/` names a requirement, `default/` a default, `seat/N` a positional seat, `gate/hand` testimony that the arg rides a person's hand (the door enforces it).
* ''`needs/` groups args by the rows themselves.'' `needs/required` stands the arg bare in the usage spine; `needs/one-of:a,b` names a choice, exactly one member riding, and the spine reads `(a | b)`; `needs/all-of:a,b,c` names a group whose members ride together or not at all, and the spine reads one bracket, members in spine order (seat order on the cli): `usage: lares ddate [+FORMAT] [<day> <month> <year>]`, never `[<day>] [<month>] [<year>]`. Every member row carries the same `needs/` value, so each row reads its group alone.
* ''Skins derive argument spellings by rule'': `cli` writes `--kebab-case`, `mcp` writes `snake_case`, `tw5` an attribute, `console` an object key. A skin row names only an exception (`maps/asking:query`).
* ''An example and a cure ride as neutral calls'' (an address and bound args), so every skin renders its own runnable line from one row. A call binding an arg a skin never takes (`skins/`, `omits/`) runs on no door of that skin, so that skin renders no line for it: the example drops there, and the refusal keeps its words without a cure. A lesson that lives in shell composition rides a literal fenced line inside `#/skins/cli`.
* ''A skin row may name more than its spelling.'' `also/` names further spellings the one door answers, comma-joined (`also/[[lares shore keep-records]]`), each routed to the same address. `door/part` marks a cli skin as one verb of a door whose other verbs keep the door's own table (`wiki filter` beside the rest of `wiki`): the spelling routes to its carrier and its own `--help` reads the carrier whole, while the door gathers no pack entry until every verb it answers holds a carrier and the door flips whole.
* ''A skin row names how a call reaches its door.'' `by/<param>` marks a spelling several carriers share (the verb word `get` skins `engine.record.reads` `by/title` and `engine.filter.pages` `by/filter`): the call picks the carrier whose `by` param it names, so the choice rests in rows a layer above may move. `handler/host` marks a door the host runs (the terminal or the seat), outside the call's registry: a call answers its bound params for the host to run. A carrier with neither a registered reactor nor `handler/host` refuses `affordance-unhandled`.
* ''A `cell` row tables one depth the door answers'' (`#/takes`, beside the args): its name holds the carry in the seed's glyphs (`?`, `*!`), `mu/` the words a shell writes (`relate`, `many-assert`), and the tagline what that depth reads. `implied/true` on a one-tool cell joins that tool to every carry that lacks its axis (a filter call reads as `*` already, so `?` there reads `*?`); `owed/<why>` tables a depth whose door answers it in a later landing, and it refuses as an empty cell. The `mu` arg itself stands once, in `#/takes/mu`.
* ''A call binds against `#/takes` as the stack resolves it.'' `default/` fills a param the call leaves out (a `needs/one-of` member's default only where no member rides), so the container defaults to `recipe/default` through this law's own `#/takes/container` row, and a layer above re-shapes the default by seating a row. A param no row names refuses `param-unknown` and names the nearest; naming two members of a `one-of` refuses `one-of-doubled`.
* The surface words read `cli` · `mcp` · `tw5` · `console`. `mcp` names the protocol every seat speaks.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ container · face · json · mu

''Shared args stand once, here.'' A carrier calls one by reference, never by copy: ``<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/container`>>``.

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes/container`>>

!!! container ~ recipe · bag · realm

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`recipe` params=`takes/slug needs/one-of:recipe,bag default/default ~ the wiki the act reads and writes; default names the worn face's daemon wiki`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/slug needs/one-of:recipe,bag ~ one bag, placed into directly; refused where this island cannot write it`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`realm` params=`takes/id ~ beside bag, the realm whose registration resolves it`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

