<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes/mu`>>

!!! mu ~ the depth of the answer

`mu` takes the seed's five pattern-match operators, each beside the word a shell carries (a nomatch shell refuses a bare `?`): `?` relate · `!` assert · `*` many · `_` dry · `0` unask. Two tools across the axes carry together (`*?` a page of has lines, `*!` a page whose rows carry their lines, `_?` a dry summary, `_!` a dry diff), written in glyphs or in words joined by a dash (`many-relate`). Two on one axis (`*_`, `?!`) answer the first tool's depth and name the second as the next call, under `mu.next`. `0` beside a tool reads as the empty hand. With no `mu`, the door's own default stands (a read's gradient). Mu names depth alone and never repeats a param: `filter` already means many, `match` already adds lines.

Each carrier tables the depths it answers as `cell` rows in its own `#/takes`; a carry outside its table refuses `mu-cell-empty` and names the nearest cell as a call, or the plain call with no `mu`.

''Dry previews every write and act.'' A carry holding `_` walks the door's whole law (every fence, the ocap, the base, the family law) to the last step and lands nothing: `_` and `_?` answer what the real call would land, the bag and layer, and `needs` (the base it takes); `_!` adds `diff`, each record it would move with its fields before and after and its text line by line. A dry answer carries the carrier's seat hints (`hints`: its `#/gate` rows and any `signs` row). A door that walks no dry path refuses a dry carry `mu-cell-empty` and names the plain call, whatever a layer above tables.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`mu` params=`takes/depth skins/console ~ the depth: relate ?, assert !, many *, dry _, unask 0; the carrier's cell rows table what each reads`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/loop`>>

!! loop ~ an act record by declaration

A carrier declares its act shape or declares none. A `#/loop` slot calls the slot of the law that owns the procedure (``<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/oracle-loop#/loop`>>``), and that slot's rows name each act slot, its phase, its writer, what the house fills there (`fills/`) and what the seat owes (`owes/`). The presence of `#/loop` decides whether a run lands an act record; nobody keeps a list of procedural affordances.

A verb that lands an act record MUST read its slot names, their order and their asks from the procedure's rows as the caller's stack seats them (the carrier that answers the address, a working layer's above canon's), the baked pack the floor, and MUST hold no procedure prose of its own. The act's answer names the carrier slot whose rows shaped it. The act record tags the affordance address, lands once at the act, and fills by slot append through the one tiddler door (a slot append needs no base).

<<~/ahu>>

